My top three confusions, in order of how much they'd worry me if I were really Dinis in the cab:

1. **Buttons that just don't respond.** Three separate times (a checklist receipt's "Done," an onboarding tour's "Skip," and "Close"/"My records" right after filing my time card) a clearly-visible button silently ate every tap with no error on screen. I only got past them by screenshotting and tapping raw pixel coordinates, or by reopening the app by URL — neither of which a real driller would think to try.
2. **Fields that look filled in but aren't saved.** The rig checklist's "starting hours" showed 3888 the whole time, but the filed record came back with "Starting hours: —" because I never retyped it. The exact same trap sits on the drill log's end-of-day meter field.
3. **A momentarily wrong hours calculation.** After typing my clock-in/out times on the time card, "ST" briefly showed 14.6 instead of 8.0 for an 8-hour shift, self-correcting only after a second edit — if I'd filed right then, I'd have signed a wrong number with no warning.

